  ( @ [mustang7757](https://forums.androidcentral.com/member.php?u=2910658), OP has a Pixel 7 Pro.)
  
  That's clearly not normal, but I would suspect some 3rd party app is causing the problem, rather than an issue with Gboard. It doesn't have to be spammy app to cause glitchiness.
  
  First, see if the problem persists in Safe Mode: [https://support.google.com/pixelphone/answer/2852139?hl=en](https://support.google.com/pixelphone/answer/2852139?hl=en). If it goes away, then something you installed is causing the problem -- you may have to uninstall apps one by one to figure out the culprit. Considering how buggy Meta apps tend to be, I'd start with Facebook and any related apps.
  
  If the problem persists, then try also uninstalling updates to Android System Webview, because sometimes updates to this can cause various glitches on only certain devices. Or if you're on the Beta for Android System Webview, leave it and revert to the stable version.
  
